1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,090
Thorndyke's.

2
00:00:01,090 --> 00:00:02,442
Good morning.

3
00:00:02,442 --> 00:00:04,360
Is that Mr Thorndyke?

4
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:04,410
Speaking.

5
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:06,230
How can I help?

6
00:00:06,230 --> 00:00:10,520
I've got quite a few things which need painting and fixing in the flat

7
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:13,890
and I wonder whether you'd be able to do the work.

8
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:17,381
I'm sure I'd be able to help but let me take down a few

9
00:00:17,381 --> 00:00:17,630
details.

10
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:19,090
Yes, of course.

11
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:22,630
Well, firstly, how did you hear about us?

12
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:24,636
It was my friend May Hampton ...

13
00:00:24,636 --> 00:00:28,647
you did some excellent work for her a couple of years ago.

14
00:00:28,647 --> 00:00:29,650
Do you remember?

15
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:30,474
Oh, yes,

16
00:00:30,474 --> 00:00:33,770
that was in West Park Flats, lovely lady.

17
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:35,080
Yes, she is.

18
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,300
And what's your name, please?

19
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:39,290
It's Edith Pargetter.

20
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:39,849
Edith ...

21
00:00:39,849 --> 00:00:43,200
can you spell your surname, please?

22
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:49,040
It's P-A-R-G-E-double T-E-R.

23
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:50,108
Double T, right.

24
00:00:50,108 --> 00:00:53,670
And do you live in West Park Flats as well?

25
00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:58,070
No, actually it's East Park, Flat 4.

26
00:00:58,070 --> 00:00:58,737
Oh, right,

27
00:00:58,737 --> 00:01:03,070
that's over the road, I seem to remember - quite difficult to get to.

28
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:03,436
Yes.

29
00:01:03,436 --> 00:01:06,000
it's at the back of the library.

30
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,324
Right, I know.

31
00:01:07,324 --> 00:01:09,530
And what's your phone number?

32
00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:17,120
875934 but I'm out a great deal in the afternoons and evenings.

33
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:20,390
So would the best time to ring you be in the morning?

34
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:21,230
Yes.

35
00:01:21,230 --> 00:01:21,557
Fine.

36
00:01:21,557 --> 00:01:23,518
I've made a note of that.

37
00:01:23,518 --> 00:01:28,093
Can I just ask, I'll be in a van and I know parking's rather

38
00:01:28,093 --> 00:01:29,400
difficult round your flats.

39
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,180
Where would you recommend?

40
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:31,533
Well.

41
00:01:31,533 --> 00:01:36,482
I always tell people in larger vehicles to Dark by the postbox on the

42
00:01:36,482 --> 00:01:39,310
other side of the road from the entrance.

43
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:41,740
Good, thanks.

44
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:44,950
And will you be able to give me a full itemised quote?

45
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:45,333
Oh.

46
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:49,160
Yes, I'll list all the jobs separately with individual prices.

47
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,900
That'd be a great help.

48
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:52,200
No problem.

49
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,570
Now, what would you like me to do?

50
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:59,570
Firstly and most urgently is in the kitchen.

51
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:03,664
With all the weather damage, the glass in the door has cracked

52
00:02:03,664 --> 00:02:05,370
and l'd need that fixing ...

53
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:07,600
I presume you mean replacing?

54
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:08,403
Oh, yes.

55
00:02:08,403 --> 00:02:10,410
And as soon as possible ...

56
00:02:10,410 --> 00:02:14,050
What I'll do is come round tomorrow morning and do that immediately.

57
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:15,788
Thank you so much.

58
00:02:15,788 --> 00:02:18,830
The other things aren't so urgent but...

59
00:02:18,830 --> 00:02:21,630
Now, I'll make a note of everything you want doing.

60
00:02:21,630 --> 00:02:25,950
Well, in the kitchen I'd like some painting doing.

61
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:28,270
All the kitchen walls?

62
00:02:28,270 --> 00:02:30,690
Just the area over the cooker.

63
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:31,900
It's very greasy ...

64
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:34,280
Right ...it does tend to get that way!

65
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,220
Yes!

66
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:40,080
Well, if you want a proper job done what I'd need to do is strip the old paint

67
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:42,780
and plaster it about a week before I paint it.

68
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:43,575
Of course.

69
00:02:43,575 --> 00:02:47,950
Now, May tells me you also do work in the garden.

70
00:02:47,950 --> 00:02:49,030
That's right.

71
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:49,436
Well.

72
00:02:49,436 --> 00:02:52,280
I'd like you to replace a fence.

73
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,460
Just one?

74
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,570
Yes, at the far end.

75
00:02:55,570 --> 00:02:55,902
Fine.

76
00:02:55,902 --> 00:02:57,230
Shouldn't be a problem.

77
00:02:57,230 --> 00:02:58,960
And that's the lot.

78
00:02:58,960 --> 00:02:59,264
Fine.

79
00:02:59,264 --> 00:03:03,522
Yeah, as I say I can come round tomorrow morning to look over things

80
00:03:03,522 --> 00:03:04,130
with you.

81
00:03:04,130 --> 00:03:05,800
That's great, thank you.

82
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,000
So, I'll look forward to seeing you tomorrow at...
